+# R0007 affected public-consumer delivery preparation
+
+The independently reviewed executable, cases and workflow are included in this R0007 candidate at the paths below. No public request, browser, provider call or delivery workflow has been executed by this tool. `request.template.json` remains UNBOUND and cannot authorize or execute acquisition; the actual triggering `request.json` is absent.
+
+## Reviewed implementation and committed placement
+
+| Preparation file | Committed repository path |
+| --- | --- |
+| `r0007_public_consumer.py` | `tools/qualification/r0007_public_consumer.py` |
+| `r0007_public_cases.json` | `tools/qualification/r0007_public_cases.json` |
+| `r0007_font_observer.js` | `tools/cp9/r0007_font_observer.js` (exact reuse of root's R0007-owned helper) |
+| `r0007-public-delivery.yml` | `.github/workflows/r0007-public-delivery.yml` |
+| `delivery-request.template.json` | `docs/state-contracts/evidence/R0007/delivery/request.template.json`; copy and bind as `request.json` only after the actual terminal prerequisites |
+
+The exact executable, case data and workflow were independently reviewed before inclusion. The integration manifest records their unchanged bytes and the path-only test adaptation. Keep the real request absent until actual owner approval, actual merge and exact-commit Pages readback have occurred. The workflow trigger is only a request-file push to the commissioned branch; it does not run on source changes or normal merge. The job's first gate rejects an unbound or premature request before dependency installation or browsers. The schema/status strings preserve gate evidence; they do not manufacture authority or independently prove the owner approved.
+
+The standalone tool imports Playwright and opens HTTP only in acquisition mode after all gates and local immutable Git identities pass. `--validate-only --template` is pure preparation and returns PREPARED_TEMPLATE_NOT_EXECUTABLE. A bound request compares probe/case/font-observer hashes with the actual local files and their copies in the merged Git tree. The explicit `--font-observer` argument is mandatory, and the request's `fontObserverSha256` binds the exact dependency. It verifies real commit objects for approved base, approved head and merged main, their exact declared trees, base ancestry of head, and ordered merge parents `[approved base, approved head]`. The intended method is expressly `merge`; squash/rebase are outside this route. The approved head tree must equal the actual merged tree. A changed tree or moved base requires explicit reconciliation before this route can accept it. Object checks do not recreate the external owner's approval authority.
+
+## Bounded public cases and non-claims
+
+Default acquisition is four independent contexts per engine, sequential Chromium and Firefox:
+
+| Case | Controlled input and actual consumer predicate |
+| --- | --- |
+| `public-reordered24` | UTC 7 September 2026, 23:00; current Isha00:30, next-day Isha00:31. Actual completed receipt and DOM must agree on Isha,00:31,next date08-09-2026,UTC,epoch1788827460000,91minutes, literal `1h 31m left until Isha`, selected row/arc marker and compatible wall interval. |
+| `public-ordinary24` | Same UTC epoch with ordinary19:30 Isha. Actual receipt/DOM must select next-day Fajr05:00,epoch1788843600000,360minutes and literal `6h 0m left until Fajr`, with ordinary wall progress/arc semantics retained. |
+| `public-missing24` | Current record admitted, actual next-day HTTP response intentionally held before headers. Countdown must remain unavailable with no fabricated target/highlight; current timetable/date/arc stay present. This is absence of an admitted next record while ingress is pending, not a claim that a real provider failed. |
+| `public-recovery24` | Same unavailable state after observable typography/render settlement, then fulfill that actual pending native request. The original fetch/JSON/adoption path must eventually paint the coherent Isha91 endpoint at the identical frozen epoch under native scheduling. Private dirty flags and exclusive wakeup causality are not observed. |
+
+`public-reordered-offline` is an optional representative offline HTML consumer, explicitly selected with `--case-id`; it is not part of the default denominator. The offline file's delivered bytes are always checked regardless of this optional behavior case.
+
+Inputs/oracles were copied from the already-authored independent R0007 recipes, not generated from observed product results. The case manifest retains its source-recipe SHA. The only pre-boot clock change is a fixed Date ingress; performance, rAF, timers, renderer, boot, state adoption, and stored product data are not replaced or invoked by the probe. Every case uses a new private browser context with explicit coordinates and no granted permissions. It reads actual public HTML unchanged and never calls render/model or seeds a product record/cache. Browser-owned storage is ephemeral, separate from the user's profile.
+
+Provider HTTP responses are controlled before provider contact, using strict expected host/path/date/coordinates/method/school matching and native JSON consumption. Weather/radar requests fail through controlled ingress. Missing/recovery hold a response before headers; this narrower boundary is explicit and does not claim the historical body-stall timing subproof. Allowlisted actual site assets and the real source font CSS/font hosts use Playwright's ordinary `route.fetch(max_redirects=0)` followed by fulfillment with that original API response. Every HTTP redirect is refused before any redirect hop. There is no `route.continue_` escape; service workers are blocked and unknown external requests/WebSockets are blocked and recorded as nonpassing evidence. Original HTTP payload bytes are preserved, but this transport buffers responses and changes ingress timing. It is not a fully uninstrumented public network timing experiment.
+
+Readiness samples and prayer-DOM MutationObserver callbacks read `window.qaState().render`, the actual last completed render receipt, plus actual DOM. `qaState()` also computes other diagnostics and may touch a pending Moon getter; before/after material classes/href are retained, and diagnostic surface changes receive no scene-preservation credit. The probe never treats the diagnostic recomputation as a painted frame. Before unavailable-state capture/recovery release, it requires the authored font LINK's genuine trusted load/error receipt; successful load also requires its actual sheet, enabled state and authored `media=all`. It forces read-only geometry and awaits the real `document.fonts.ready` promise. Readiness alone does not prove the later font-event dispatch has completed. The exact R0007-owned early observer must also admit each relevant terminal face through its own typed `loadingdone`/`loadingerror` event and a captured native zero-timer receipt after dispatch. Missing receipts, outstanding deferred tasks, observed removal/restart or descriptor mutation fail closed. The observer is concatenated before the public INIT in one `add_init_script` call to guarantee installation order. The tool then observes unchanged actual render/geometry/font signatures across three native rAF callbacks, checking current observer settlement after each layout read and after final screenshot geometry. It repeats settlement before final capture. This is a static authored startup lifecycle protocol, not a universal future-font quiescence claim; a legitimate cached loaded face with no terminal event is conservatively unverified. These observations truthfully report `dirtyState: not-exposed`: neither the private dirty flag nor private loop state is accessible through the public diagnostics. The real 250ms wait plus subsequent settlement supports eventual recovery only; other natural wakeups are not excluded. No earliest/all-first-presented-frame claim, full-scene motion/Moon acceptance, exclusive-wakeup claim, or live-provider incidence is made.
+
+Acquisition credit is assigned only after successful actual observation export, required checkpoint membership, nonempty structurally complete PNG/WebM files, exact snapshot/receipt/geometry/screenshot-digest presentation bindings, browser identity and returned owned close calls. PNG structure/CRC/scanline and WebM bounded-element/track/block checks detect missing, malformed or truncated artifacts; actual frame decoding and pixel meaning remain independently reviewed. Launch entry, returned handles and every SDK close call are recorded. A launch exception before a handle returns has unknown process custody, even if no close call was possible; later acquisitions stop. SDK closure receipts do not claim an independent OS process census. Every attempted case retains its trace on failure, and producer exit remains nonzero for failed/unverified acquisition.
+
+## Pre-approval readiness and exact approval request
+
+1. Reconcile the whole-owner ledger against latest accepted main after the preceding R0017 corrective changes are accepted into main, preserving the authorized R0017→R0007→R000B merge order. Current source, all still-applicable original duties, ES07, source/generated parity and relevant native Linux/Windows qualifications must be accounted for. Keep owner-assigned exceptions exact.
+2. Finish executable engineering, fix independently reviewed findings, and bind the separately attributed review to exact PR head/base/tree. Inspect whole diff/generated files and artifact/source hashes. These helper files are now included through the reviewed source process; freeze the final candidate identities and prepare a certificate with delivery fields explicitly pending.
+3. Read current PR via `github_get_pr_info` and checks via `github_get_commit_combined_status`; verify exact head/base/tree, completed review and all required readiness. Request the single owner's merge decision with those exact identities. State AWAITING_OWNER_MERGE_APPROVAL. A reviewed PR is not whole-owner completion.
+
+## Post-approval same-thread merge and delivery sequence
+
+1. Bind the actual owner approval receipt to the exact candidate and agreed `merge` method. Re-read PR head/base/mergeability/checks and current main; do not promote approval across a changed candidate/base without reconciliation. Use `github_merge_pull_request(repository_full_name=theislampill/salah_widget, pr_number=<actual>, expected_head_sha=<approved head>, merge_method=merge)`. The tool has a head guard but no base guard, so current-base readback immediately before merge remains necessary. Inspect a rejection or uncertain result before replaying the effect.
+2. Read back merged PR and merge commit with `github_get_pr_info` / `github_fetch_commit`; bind actual main SHA/tree and source/generated hashes. Verify the issue remains open rather than assuming the non-closing Implements#7 PR closed it. Record the satisfied merge one-shot before proceeding.
+3. Inspect the normal Pages deployment associated with the exact merged main SHA. The specialized commit-workflow tool filters PR runs and is insufficient for all Pages runs. Use the existing allowed connector GET `https://api.github.com/repos/theislampill/salah_widget/actions/runs?head_sha=<merged SHA>` and inspect actual workflow/job conclusions through `github_fetch_workflow_run_jobs`; reconcile deployment/source identity outside this probe. No rerun, replacement deployment or broad polling is built in. If Pages is still pending or bytes stale, retain the exact state and wait for a real change signal.
+4. Fill the request with actual approval/head/base/head-tree/base-tree receipt, verified `merge` method/main SHA/tree, successful exact-source Pages run id/receipt, expected file byte lengths/SHA256 from that immutable merged Git tree, and the reviewed probe/case digests. Only then set `status=READY_AFTER_APPROVAL_MERGE_AND_PAGES_READBACK`, approval statusAPPROVED_EXACT_CANDIDATE, merge statusMERGED_VERIFIED, and Pages statusSUCCESS_VERIFIED_EXTERNALLY. These fields record already obtained evidence, not new grants. Preserve exact owner authority separately.
+5. Publish this request only on the commissioned branch. The prepared Windows job unshallows/fetches current main's complete immutable ancestry (no tags, blob filtering), requires it to equal the requested merged SHA, and the script verifies real approved base/head/merge objects, ancestry, exact ordered parents and all expected file/helper identities before HTTP/browser acquisition. A missing object/history is a failure, not a reason to skip a check. The job is Contents-read only, private Windows2022, headed Chromium/Firefox, one owned concurrency group, and pinned checkout/upload. No R0017 workflow/runner or shared local preview is used. A request commit on the feature branch does not alter deployed main or start another Pages deployment.
+6. Download/read back the exact delivery artifact and inspect raw served hashes, actual root/config navigation identities, controlled-ingress ledgers, actual completed receipt/DOM, screenshots, original videos, browser binary/version/OS and actual producer exit. Re-read current main and the Pages binding after acquisition to detect a moved external frontier before certificate acceptance. Source assertions return only PARTIAL_INDEPENDENT_PIXELS_REQUIRED. A separately attributed actual-pixel review must close the affected visible predicates and source association. A zero process exit or the request's Pages string is not whole-owner acceptance.
+7. Complete and publish the whole-owner certificate only after every original/ES07/delivery residual is terminal under the actual owner/policy. Bind actual merge, delivered source, Pages run, public cases, independent review, original evidence/approved exceptions and remaining non-claims. Use `github_add_comment_to_issue` with the actual issue number7 (this connector names its parameter `pr_number`) and immediately read back the issue comments to verify the certificate bytes/location.
+8. When actually eligible under the approved commission, deliberately close issue7 with `github_update_issue(repository_full_name=theislampill/salah_widget, issue_number=7, state=closed, state_reason=completed)`, then `github_fetch_issue` readback of the completed state. Do not let certificate publication or mere PR merge stand in for issue closure. Finish formal audit closure from the actual evidence and continuity records; do not emit completion while a dependent gate remains pending. R000B remains its separate owner/thread.
