+# R0007 single-ref Git pack publication design
+
+## Commission and selection
+
+Root authorized local implementation after the bounded diagnosis in `../publication-second-andon/report.md`. The selected route is a normal Git push of one intermediate commit, followed by connector finalization. REST retries have failed twice; direct job publication of changed workflow files would expand the permission boundary; LFS or splitting the runtime changes the product. The selected route preserves the exact target product bytes and existing principal while explicitly allowing one owned-ref update.
+
+All source, controls, disposable fixtures and reports belong in this directory. Existing helper/candidate files remain untouched. No external writes, browser actions, credential export, force option, sibling/main ref effects or acceptance/closure authority are granted.
+
+## Fixed identities and tree equation
+
+- Repository: `theislampill/salah_widget`; Git URL: `https://github.com/theislampill/salah_widget.git`.
+- Ref: `refs/heads/pro/r0007-explicit-next-event-state-20261106`.
+- Current target baseline: commit `9d24fb4b34f5979aac9961f34794ffbf4490e049`, tree `0f0385b51b08e62a3668e8aa8e3534cadac70749`. Final preparation accepts root's explicit full immutable clean target SHA; root may advance it for separately reviewed fixture-binding changes. No final actual payload is prepared in this lane.
+- Known ancestry, immediate parent first: `3b2d09c748f71dc77806882f62f7339cbd18f19c`, `19004279805604ef5e41292ffd4e9f442e1321f2`, `eebba178172f96b3ffe5ab3845bc0fffd57c6e1b`.
+- New executing seed must have the first listed commit as its sole parent. Verify every listed edge and each seed's exact cumulative four-path delta from base. Checkout depth four.
+- Intermediate tree: exact target outside `.github/workflows/` and the three bootstrap metadata paths; exact executing-seed workflow subtree plus exact executing-seed bytes/modes for all four bootstrap files.
+- Intermediate commit: sole parent executing seed. Final connector commit: exact target tree, sole parent verified intermediate; precisely two target workflow additions and four bootstrap removals.
+
+## Files and interfaces
+
+`templates/materialize.py` retains source reconstruction and exact-target validation, then builds/verifies the intermediate tree and invokes `publish_intermediate(root, intermediate_commit, expected_seed, evidence, token) -> dict`. The return record contains structured publication state and readback identities; no arbitrary command response text. `build_intermediate(root, target_tree, seed, evidence) -> dict` returns the intermediate tree and six finalization paths. `validate_seed_chain(root, head, manifest, upload) -> None` checks the explicit chain; dry base reconstruction remains token/network-free.
+
+`prepare_payload.py` reads immutable local objects and writes the same four seed files plus a local preparation receipt. It binds `seedAncestors`, target tree, complete finalization path list, materializer bytes, patch and all changed blobs. Production defaults are the exact commission; fixture inputs are explicit immutable arguments. No remote endpoint can be provided by CLI or manifest.
+
+`templates/r0007-materialize.yml` uses the existing pinned actions and Contents-write permission, depth four, disabled persisted checkout credentials, and one authenticated publication call after reconstruction. Launcher evidence records unknown ref effect after an abnormal termination; it never assumes false once publication could have begun.
+
+## Push and credential boundary
+
+The implementation uses the fixed Git URL and one fully qualified refspec, normal fast-forward behavior, and no force, mirror, tag, delete, additional-ref or submodule push options. A private pre-push guard validates Git's advertised old SHA, exact new SHA, exact remote/ref and one update only. Existing pre-push hooks or hooks-path/URL-rewrite/credential configuration cause a fixed refusal; no existing security gate is overwritten or disabled.
+
+An ephemeral askpass script contains no credential. Only the authenticated Git push process environment contains the token under a dedicated variable; builders and ordinary Git children get a scrubbed environment. The script answers only the exact fixed HTTPS repository's username/password prompt, with credential path matching enabled and redirects disabled. No token enters argv, URLs, Git config, files, receipts or raw command logs. Post-push readback uses the scrubbed environment; unavailable unauthenticated readback leaves publication unverified for root, without broadening credential access.
+
+Private intent and guard receipts precede the push. Only one push call is made. Command stdout/stderr are captured in memory and reduced to byte counts/hashes and fixed classifications. Raw error text is never retained. A timeout, rejection or malformed result preserves an uncertain write outcome and stops; independent readback must decide what exists. Root remains the finalizer.
+
+## Meaningful checks and handoff
+
+Use actual disposable bare Git for a successful single-ref push and advanced, rewound, wrong-ref and multiple-update refusals. Check complete intermediate tree/workflow equality and exact six-path finalization; full chain with depth four; refusal when an existing hook/configuration would be displaced; token/config/log exclusion; and uncertain outcome without a second push. Production has no local-remote override; tests patch the module's fixed remote only in their own process.
+
+Run the focused controls and capture raw local producer results. Freeze all packet bytes and hashes for a fresh independent reviewer. Root separately performs the actual target preparation/dry rebuild and any hosted/publication action. No source/body experiment or external push occurs in this implementation lane.
