+# R0007 Git Pack Publication Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** Use superpowers:executing-plans for the scoped implementation. Root already authorized implementation and owns the subsequent independent review and remote actions.
+
+**Goal:** Transport the exact R0007 target product objects through one ordinary owned-branch Git push with explicit conditional-update and credential controls.
+
+**Architecture:** Preserve the existing reconstruction mechanism in a new helper directory. Build an exact intermediate tree, verify a private advertisement guard, push once, and retain structured uncertain/success outcomes for connector finalization.
+
+**Tech stack:** Python standard library, Git CLI, existing pinned GitHub Actions.
+
+**Spec:** `DESIGN.md` and the explicit root commission.
+
+## Global constraints
+
+Only this directory may be written. Preserve previous helper bytes as historical inputs. No active candidate edit, real remote write, force, credential export, arbitrary response logging or review/closure authority. Production remote/ref are constants. Target and seed ancestry are exact manifest bindings; no inferred latest head.
+
+## Review focus
+
+- A remote ref changes between preflight and push: advertised old-ID guard and Git receiver checks must reject.
+- A Git configuration or existing hook redirects/bypasses the intended gate: refuse without overwriting it.
+- A failed client command follows a completed server write: retain uncertainty and never retry.
+- Workflow/bootstrap paths accidentally enter the job's mutation delta: compare complete intermediate/seed/target trees.
+- A credential reaches a builder, command string, config or receipt: synthetic-token exclusion controls must detect it.
+
+## Tasks
+
+### 1. Publication boundary and local Git controls
+
+- [x] Write failing tests for `publish_intermediate(root, intermediate_commit, expected_seed, evidence, token)` and private advertised-update guard.
+- [x] Preserve the failing producer evidence.
+- [x] Implement fixed remote/ref, existing-hook/config checks, private intent/guard, ephemeral scoped askpass, single no-force push and scrubbed readback.
+- [x] Verify actual local bare-Git success; advanced/rewound/wrong/multiple-ref refusal; token exclusion; uncertainty/no replay.
+
+### 2. Exact chain, intermediate tree and seed preparation
+
+- [x] Write failing controls for `validate_seed_chain` and `build_intermediate`, including exact six-path finalization and depth-four checkout.
+- [x] Copy historical helper/preparer/workflow into this directory with input hashes.
+- [x] Bind the exact ancestor list, preserve source reconstruction, add intermediate/commit checks and structured publication summary.
+- [x] Update preparation manifest and depth-four workflow; remove unconditional false ref-effect claims from launcher.
+- [x] Verify disposable chain/tree fixture and wrong-chain/path controls.
+
+### 3. Freeze the packet
+
+- [x] Run combined focused controls and compile/parse checks; retain raw outputs and receipts.
+- [x] Inspect scope diff against preserved helper inputs and report material limitations.
+- [x] Write exact file hashes and handoff report; stop writes for root's fresh independent review.
+
+No active-repository commits are part of this analysis helper lane. Root's request to execute after a concise design/plan supplies the implementation authorization; there is no additional approval pause before local work.
