+# Bounded successor repair plan
+
+Root authorized this isolated successor after confirming a synthetic credential-file escape through Git Trace2. All writes are confined to this directory and disposable local Git fixtures. The original frozen publication-pack packet and reviewer inputs remain unchanged. No candidate, hosted, network, final payload or real ref effect is authorized here.
+
+1. Preserve original source/test hashes and supplied reviewer witness; verify all 100 original frozen files.
+2. Reproduce the original environment witness against byte-identical helper code, and add actual global-config normal/event/perf trace witnesses. Keep RED outputs and traces.
+3. Consume the bounded Andon report supplied by root. Apply the smallest scoped correction: remove controlled child-process tracing environment; refuse equivalent existing Trace2 config before credential-bearing execution, retaining configuration and existing gates.
+4. Run the new trace witnesses and the existing 23 local boundary controls. Preserve producer records and configuration/ref/credential evidence. No unrelated tests or redesign.
+5. Freeze exact source hashes, diff, report and packet for root's independent successor review; stop writes.
+
+The endpoint/ref, manifest/tree/ancestry, normal single-push, hook security, TLS, credential authority and uncertainty behavior remain fixed. Existing Git configuration is not edited or disabled. Actual candidate preparation and all publication remain root-owned.
+
+Completed: all five steps are evidenced in HANDOFF.md, scope-verification.json and the frozen packet. Writes stop after packet generation.
